learnings:
  - 'Truncated delegation final-reports are a recurring pattern in long builder runs. Mitigation: verify file-existence + compliance independently after each delegation; treat the final report as a hint not a contract.'
  - The CLI-verb-first then UI-on-top design pattern works — the verbs become library functions the UI calls. No work is wasted; what changes is the consumer.
  - v1 readiness is gated on actual creator workflow validation (drag-drop in browser, agent end-to-end), not CLI-completeness. Per TD-2026-05-27-723 (local-only-by-default), the test surface should validate via local whisper + agents, not online fallbacks.
